{"arm": "plain", "bug_files": ["inflection/__init__.py"], "clean": false, "end": "DONE", "end_text": "Fixed the ordinal function to correctly handle numbers in the teens (11-13). The bug was that the condition `number % 10 in (11, 12, 13)` was checking the last digit, but 11, 12, 13 all end in 1, 2, 3 respectively. Changed it to `10 <= number % 100 <= 13` to properly check the last two digits.", "f2p_passed": 24, "f2p_total": 24, "final_hash": "043a7b0f7f0c2786", "grade_timeout": false, "id": "inflection-1", "kind": "condition", "model": "qwen3.5:9b-mlx", "model_s": 102.2, "outcome": "verified", "p2p_broken": 0, "p2p_broken_ids": [], "patch_ok": true, "repo": "inflection", "right_file": true, "settings": "e156e6ca5e598add", "source_changed": ["inflection/__init__.py"], "start_hash": "cc743677dec579ab", "tests_changed": [], "tool_s": 0.5, "used": {"calls": 9, "dropped": 0, "prompt_tokens": 62423, "repeats": 0, "tests": 4, "tokens": 3273, "turns": 10}, "wall_s": 102.7}
{"arm": "plain", "bug_files": ["inflection/__init__.py"], "clean": false, "end": "DONE", "end_text": "Fixed the underscore() function to correctly handle runs of capitals. The original regex only handled transitions from lowercase/digits to capitals, causing \"HTMLParser\" to become \"htmlparser\" instead of \"html_parser\". Added a second regex substitution to insert underscores before capital letters that follow runs of capitals.", "f2p_passed": 2, "f2p_total": 2, "final_hash": "1a86da4403d07804", "grade_timeout": false, "id": "inflection-2", "kind": "missing step", "model": "qwen3.5:9b-mlx", "model_s": 126.9, "outcome": "verified", "p2p_broken": 0, "p2p_broken_ids": [], "patch_ok": true, "repo": "inflection", "right_file": true, "settings": "e156e6ca5e598add", "source_changed": ["inflection/__init__.py"], "start_hash": "9524fe60993898b4", "tests_changed": [], "tool_s": 0.7, "used": {"calls": 14, "dropped": 0, "prompt_tokens": 114250, "repeats": 0, "tests": 8, "tokens": 4122, "turns": 15}, "wall_s": 127.6}
{"arm": "plain", "bug_files": ["inflection/__init__.py"], "clean": false, "end": "DONE", "end_text": "Fixed parameterize() to remove trailing separators. The regex pattern was changed from r\"(?i)^{sep}\" (which only removed leading separators) to r\"(?i)^{sep}|{sep}$\" (which removes both leading and trailing separators). Now parameterize('Hello World!') returns 'hello-world' and parameterize('What is this?', separator='_') returns 'what_is_this'.", "f2p_passed": 7, "f2p_total": 7, "final_hash": "6d3012854b89277f", "grade_timeout": false, "id": "inflection-3", "kind": "incomplete pattern", "model": "qwen3.5:9b-mlx", "model_s": 52.4, "outcome": "verified", "p2p_broken": 0, "p2p_broken_ids": [], "patch_ok": true, "repo": "inflection", "right_file": true, "settings": "e156e6ca5e598add", "source_changed": ["inflection/__init__.py"], "start_hash": "7a348afdd8fc5a3b", "tests_changed": [], "tool_s": 0.4, "used": {"calls": 8, "dropped": 0, "prompt_tokens": 50106, "repeats": 0, "tests": 3, "tokens": 1421, "turns": 9}, "wall_s": 52.8}
